<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krasnaya Polyana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krasnaya Polyana is a mountain settlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sochi">Sochi</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Krasnodar</a> Krai, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the site of the Circassian locality of Kbaada. There, on 21 May 1864, Russian forces held a victory parade marking the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-circassian-war">Russo-Circassian War</a>. Today it is a ski resort that hosted the mountain events of the 2014 Winter Olympics.</p></div>
